        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 rounded-2xl p-8 text-gray-200">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="mb-4">
            Acid etching is a chemical gamble that pays off only on soft, porous, unsealed concrete, and most garage floors are none of those things. Grinding is a mechanical certainty. It removes the paste, the sealer, the old paint and the tire polish in one pass and leaves the uniform CSP 2 to 3 profile that every coating manufacturer actually asks for.
          </p>
          <p class="m-0">
            The kit says etch because the kit has to be easy to sell. The installer grinds because the installer has to come back if it fails. Rent the grinder, wear the respirator, and do the job once.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
